cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "A Priori Power Analysis Wizard"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Atzori"
    given-names: "Federico"
    affiliation: "University of Cagliari"
version: 1.5.3
date-released: 2026-08-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/federicoatz/apriori-power-wizard"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21804595
# The identifiers below pin two different things, and both are needed.
# The CONCEPT DOI always resolves to the most recent archived release, and
# is what a general citation of "the software" should use. The VERSION DOI
# pins the exact snapshot this file's `version:` field declares, which is
# what anyone reproducing a specific result needs.
#
# Zenodo mints the version DOI a few minutes after a GitHub RELEASE (not a
# tag -- a tag alone is invisible to it), so it can only be filled in as a
# follow-up edit, never in the release commit itself. It had gone stale
# three times before; the fix was to stop relying on memory and make every
# tag a release. If you add a release, come back and update the value
# below, and check paper.tex's matching Zenodo citations in the same pass.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21804595
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest archived release"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21970298
    description: "Archived snapshot of version 1.5.3 on Zenodo"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21894025
    description: "Archived snapshot of version 1.5.2 on Zenodo"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21844125
    description: "Archived snapshot of version 1.4.3, the version described in the accompanying working paper"
abstract: >-
  A step-by-step Shiny application that guides researchers in experimental
  economics and behavioral science through an a priori (before data
  collection) power analysis to determine required sample size, without
  assuming prior power-analysis experience.
keywords:
  - power analysis
  - sample size
  - experimental economics
  - behavioral science
  - R Shiny
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A Priori Power Analysis Wizard: A Guided Interface for Choosing and
      Justifying Sample-Size Calculations in Behavioral Science
    authors:
      - family-names: "Atzori"
        given-names: "Federico"
        affiliation: "University of Cagliari"
    url: "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=7247658"
    notes: >-
      Working paper describing the design and validation of this software;
      posted to SSRN, revised 2026-08-07; not yet peer-reviewed.
